    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d448-a1">

                <pb facs="0769" n="1727" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1727"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 7.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Sackville to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-10-27"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 27,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Personal.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear</hi> Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                    >Bayard</hi>: Referring to an interview which is reported in the New York
                    Tribune of the 24th instant, I remark that my words are so turned as to impugn
                    the action of the Executive. I beg to emphasize that I had no thought or
                    intention of doing so, and I most, emphatically deny the language which is
                    attributed to me by other papers of “clap-trap” and “trickery,” as applied to
                    the Government to which I am accredited. My record here has been, I trust, such
                    as to preclude the possibility of my having used such language, but I must, I
                    suppose, succumb to the consequences of having been made a victim to an infamous
                    plot.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sackville.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
